      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for simplifying this, the previous code was hard to follow.\n\nCan you add text to the commit message to explain why this is correct? I believe the reason is that Tethering initializes mBpfCoordinator just once in the constructor. After that point, the value of isUsingBpf can never change, because mIsBpfEnabled is final and mBpfCoordinatorShim.isInitialized() is either always true (api30) or can either never change (api31).\n\nAlso please look at the comment about removing mUsingBpfOffload. I think its existence is confusing (and buggy) and hopefully we can remove it.",
      "revId": "820d2d9a7b172b0e8c43110812cc791264c208a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
