      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T14:45:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can just change this to mBpfCoordinator.isUsingBpf() and remove mUsingBpfOffload entirely?\n\nIt currently seems to be possible for BpfCoordinator to be started with BPF disabled (when Tethering starts), but then for the configuration to change to enable BPF (e.g., because the OVERRIDE_TETHER_ENABLE_BPF_OFFLOAD flag changed). From that point on any new IpServer created will have mUsingBpfOffload \u003d true and will start an IpNeighborMonitor. This won\u0027t work, because BpfCoordinator has BPF disabled.\n\nRemoving mUsingBpfOffload entirely would fix this.",
